  "body": "Follow-up of #2597.\n\nThe fix for #2597 cuts a new, larger outline from Top Z down, one stepdown at a time. The contour generator gets no stock region. So it takes the material outside the part to stand up to Top Z.\n\nWhere the stock is narrow, the added passes cut air. This is safe, but it costs time.\n\nProposal:\n- Give the stock region (the stock outline at each level) to the whole-model contour.\n- Start each new ring at the first level where its tool sweep meets stock that is not cut.\n- Keep the refusal by name when a ring cannot be proven clear.\n\nFiles: `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole_reach.rs` (`reach_up`), and the app code that builds `ContourParams`.\n\nThis work is under the safety floor: it can change posted G-code.\n",
